1
00:00:01,088 --> 00:00:07,829
AI agents now sign payments, approvals and permits on their own. One bad signature can empty a wallet.

2
00:00:08,288 --> 00:00:16,117
presign-guard checks it first. Send what your agent is about to sign, and get back green, orange or red, with the reasons.

3
00:00:16,591 --> 00:00:20,900
An unlimited token approval? Orange: ask a person before you sign.

4
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:26,709
A permit that hands a plain wallet your tokens? Red. That is how most wallet drainers work.

5
00:00:27,172 --> 00:00:32,143
And a normal x402 payment? Green. It moves one fixed amount, once.

6
00:00:32,604 --> 00:00:47,495
Agents pay one cent per check, with x402 or MPP: USDC on Base, Solana or Algorand, RLUSD on the XRP Ledger, or a Tempo session. The verdict comes back in the same request.

7
00:00:47,954 --> 00:00:57,746
Your agent can also say what it means to do, like swap ten USDC for ETH. If the transaction does something else, presign-guard flags it.

8
00:00:58,214 --> 00:01:07,430
New: presign-guard also runs the transaction first. A hidden approval, an NFT leaving the wallet, or a transaction that would fail: orange.

9
00:01:07,896 --> 00:01:16,088
Paying an x402 API? Send along what the seller asked for. A signature that pays more, or pays someone else, is red.

10
00:01:16,551 --> 00:01:22,418
Errors are never charged. And if a data source is down, there is no verdict, never a guessed green.

11
00:01:22,879 --> 00:01:25,375
presign-guard. Check it before you sign it.

